# Festag — keine kleinen Texte unter Titeln

Do **not** put small support / subtitle / Zwischenüberschrift paragraphs under titles.

## Forbidden

- `p` under `h1` / AuthGlassyHero (e.g. `.wc-os-support`, `.wc-hero-support`, `.set-page-lead`, page leads)
- A short label title + separate muted explanation line underneath
- Extra “helper” sentences under the title that are not part of the H1 itself

## Correct pattern

**One title element only** — `AuthGlassyHero` (or equivalent):

- **Lead** = dark ink (light mode) / soft white (dark mode)
- **Rest** = muted gray, same H1 size, same sentence flow
- Max **3 sentences** in the title total (often 1–2)
- No second text node under the title for “explanation”

```tsx
<AuthGlassyHero
  lead="Erstelle deinen Workspace."
  rest="Wähle einen Namen und wie du ihn nutzen willst."
/>
```

Not:

```tsx
<h1>Erstelle deinen Workspace.</h1>
<p className="…-support">Every workspace is an independent…</p>
```

## Also still applies

- `festag-no-page-leads` — no leads under page `h1` on routes
- `festag-no-kickers` — no uppercase eyebrows
- Popup H1 may be 1–3 calm sentences **inside** the title; body T1 is for modal *content* after the title, not a second title line

When touching auth, onboarding, workspace create, or any titled surface: remove leftover support paragraphs — do not reintroduce them.
